{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1434428-wyld-shaping-technique-heaven-weaving-new-soul-into-the-loom-of-fate-2nd-ed","id":1434428,"title":"Wyld-Shaping Technique: Heaven weaving new soul into the Loom of Fate (2nd Ed)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-02-03T16:02:56-08:00","id":1434428,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon14.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Wyld-Shaping Technique: Heaven weaving new soul into the Loom of Fate (2nd Ed)","content":"Lets say I want to make people with souls that will continue on after their deaths. Wyld-Shaping Technique does not allow this by itself because the new, Wyld-Shaped soul is not woven into the Loom of Fate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted 2nd Ed Core Book, Wyld-Shaping Technique, p.g. 217</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creatures made using Wyld-Shaping Technique are outside Creation\u2019s processes of life and death. They do not reincarnate in Creation or as a real creature unless Heaven orders their pattern woven into the Loom of Fate. Nor do they form ghosts unless the Neverborn intervene to recreate their Essence pattern as such. They fade away upon their deaths and are no longer valid targets for Charms or other effects unless otherwise stated.</div> </div> </div> </div>So how do I go about that?<br /> <br /> Or, does Wyld Cauldron Technology (WCT) automatically make these souls permanent? I find the wording vague. WCT specifically discuses altering existing people, but not specifically making the souls of Wyld-Shaped people permanent.<br /> <br /> If Wyld Cauldron Tech. does not make these souls permanent, how do you weave their souls' pattern into the Loom of Fate?<br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy?<br /> <br /> Sidereal Charm I've missed?<br /> <br /> Astrology or Craft-Fate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4428,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","user":"Daredevil","date":". 02-03-2021, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T17:01:57-08:00","id":1434434,"title":"","content":"It would be astrology which is also done through craft:fate. In order to weave the pattern into the loom you'd probably have to petition a god to get the pattern spiders to do it unless you know a sidereal willing to do it for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T18:37:27-08:00","id":1434443,"title":"","content":"could the Solars develop a custom E6+ charm to do it? or should it stay entirely out of their power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T19:21:48-08:00","id":1434446,"title":"","content":"You could talk to the psychopomp gods in the Bureau of Endings and convince them to do it. Sounds right up their alley.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T21:08:48-08:00","id":1434454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1434428-wyld-shaping-technique-heaven-weaving-new-soul-into-the-loom-of-fate-2nd-ed?p=1434443#post1434443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">could the Solars develop a custom E6+ charm to do it? or should it stay entirely out of their power?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thematically, it's out of their power. Crafting things into and out of fate is the purview of sidereals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T04:37:48-08:00","id":1434470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1434428-wyld-shaping-technique-heaven-weaving-new-soul-into-the-loom-of-fate-2nd-ed?p=1434454#post1434454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thematically, it's out of their power. Crafting things into and out of fate is the purview of sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd think so, but as I recall, so much of their charmset was based on something being inside fate already that it really screwed them when abyssals and internals were outside of fate by default. <br /> <br /> As far as I know they had no published power to overcome this issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T05:05:36-08:00","id":1434472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1434428-wyld-shaping-technique-heaven-weaving-new-soul-into-the-loom-of-fate-2nd-ed?p=1434443#post1434443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">could the Solars develop a custom E6+ charm to do it? or should it stay entirely out of their power?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why not, actually. Since 2e had A Hood on Death for Solars to conquer disease by converting a vast swathe of disease into a loyal disease god, I don't think it's out of the question for a Solar to conceptualise &quot;conquering life and death&quot; by creating new human souls. Perhaps in a similar way to the Infernal charm Spawning Pit Sanctification?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26460-organ-boy","name":"Organ Boy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T06:53:18-08:00","id":1434488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1434428-wyld-shaping-technique-heaven-weaving-new-soul-into-the-loom-of-fate-2nd-ed?p=1434470#post1434470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You'd think so, but as I recall, so much of their charmset was based on something being inside fate already that it really screwed them when abyssals and internals were outside of fate by default.<br /> <br /> As far as I know they had no published power to overcome this issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can still use craft:fate on the loom. Which while underdefined would still allow an ability like this to happen. They can also use Of Horror's Best Unknown to do it but that's really only for things that are really outside fate to pull them. For example a 3rd circle demon or deathlord.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 02-04-2021, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T06:54:14-08:00","id":1434489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1434428-wyld-shaping-technique-heaven-weaving-new-soul-into-the-loom-of-fate-2nd-ed?p=1434470#post1434470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You'd think so, but as I recall, so much of their charmset was based on something being inside fate already that it really screwed them when abyssals and internals were outside of fate by default. </div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. The limits of Sidereals against characters outside of Fate were clearly defined, and just a few things to do with affecting Willpower or mental influence.<br /> <br /> And that was only for Charms with the Fate Keyword, which were not many.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T11:29:38-08:00","id":1434506,"title":"","content":"I think in first edition it explicitly just kinda happened if they existed in the world for a while -- months or years bumping up literally and metaphorically against other real things, influencing and being influenced, causes the fate of a Wyld-shaped person or thing to tangle up with and then be woven into the loom of fate.<br /> <br /> I don't have a cite, though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T12:17:58-08:00","id":1434513,"title":"","content":"It's a big project though, as a Solar you'd need to convince a significant majority of the Sidereals that your crafted people are worth keeping around in Creation. Presumably as other Solars are making their own, similar requests.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the bitterest and most bloody battles of the First Age were over whose OCs would be made canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T13:02:15-08:00","id":1434518,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Yeah, I'm just checking back over the First Edition version of Sidereals, and it explicitly limits effects that cannot work on beings outside Fate to affecting their Willpower levels (including positively), compelling behaviour and transportation between locations. It notably does not prevent them from predicting such beings futures.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Heck, that Edition's version of Conclusive Wisdom waives the usual limits to allow it to still affect higher circle demons.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Second Edition errata limited that even further, just making it so that such beings did not have their memories altered by reality altering Charms. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1434428-wyld-shaping-technique-heaven-weaving-new-soul-into-the-loom-of-fate-2nd-ed?p=1434513#post1434513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a big project though</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you basing that on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T14:07:45-08:00","id":1434526,"title":"","content":"ya, a sidereal could do it, they have a charm for it - prayers to the pattern spiders might also do it (if your ST allows) and craft:fate could also do it, if you know how to do that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T16:19:23-08:00","id":1434539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1434428-wyld-shaping-technique-heaven-weaving-new-soul-into-the-loom-of-fate-2nd-ed?p=1434518#post1434518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are you basing that on?</div> </div> </div> </div>My desire to make a joke about Solars being fanfic nerds and Fate being analogous to a fandom's Canon.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T04:08:41-08:00","id":1434578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1434428-wyld-shaping-technique-heaven-weaving-new-soul-into-the-loom-of-fate-2nd-ed?p=1434506#post1434506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in first edition it explicitly just kinda happened if they existed in the world for a while -- months or years bumping up literally and metaphorically against other real things, influencing and being influenced, causes the fate of a Wyld-shaped person or thing to tangle up with and then be woven into the loom of fate.<br /> <br /> I don't have a cite, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's what I remembered. As the created wyld-beings and wyld-terrain interacted with those who were part of Creation proper, those things slowly also became subsumed into the Loom, the people there gained souls, and all of that became indistinguishable from places that had always been a part of Creation. You didn't need to go talk with a Sidereal or a god and ask them to give these people souls and attach them to the Loom of Fate. As long as they had constant contact with the people and things of Creation proper, that would all happen on its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T17:23:54-08:00","id":1434649,"title":"","content":"On a <i>somewhat</i> related note:<br /> <br /> The Arczeckhi had the quaint belief that only physical force and spiritual might were real, and only acknowledged someone as a person after they murdered someone else.<br /> <br /> I always felt that their culture could have begun with wyld-shaped people who had been told about the stitch but <i>maybe</i> got a few details wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T21:54:35-08:00","id":1434666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1434428-wyld-shaping-technique-heaven-weaving-new-soul-into-the-loom-of-fate-2nd-ed?p=1434578#post1434578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's what I remembered. As the created wyld-beings and wyld-terrain interacted with those who were part of Creation proper, those things slowly also became subsumed into the Loom, the people there gained souls, and all of that became indistinguishable from places that had always been a part of Creation. You didn't need to go talk with a Sidereal or a god and ask them to give these people souls and attach them to the Loom of Fate. As long as they had constant contact with the people and things of Creation proper, that would all happen on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember correctly, took at least a year and a day but I could be misremembering. Whether that matters or not I guess depends on the context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T04:58:04-08:00","id":1435174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1434428-wyld-shaping-technique-heaven-weaving-new-soul-into-the-loom-of-fate-2nd-ed?p=1434666#post1434666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I remember correctly, took at least a year and a day but I could be misremembering. Whether that matters or not I guess depends on the context.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically everything was &quot;a year and a day&quot; or &quot;until Calibration&quot;, so it would make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T07:58:37-08:00","id":1435197,"title":"","content":"Somehow &quot;a year and a day&quot; loses a bit of its poetry when it's 451 days rather than 366.<br /> <br /> Although... if we include Calibration, that would make it 456... I could see an artistry to that numerical sequence. Yes, never mind then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T09:23:09-08:00","id":1435210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1434428-wyld-shaping-technique-heaven-weaving-new-soul-into-the-loom-of-fate-2nd-ed?p=1435197#post1435197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Somehow &quot;a year and a day&quot; loses a bit of its poetry when it's 451 days rather than 366.<br /> <br /> Although... if we include Calibration, that would make it 456... I could see an artistry to that numerical sequence. Yes, never mind then.</div> </div> </div> </div>421/426 now. Months are Lunar Months now: down to 28 days (four weeks). (15 x 28) + 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T10:25:57-08:00","id":1436036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1434428-wyld-shaping-technique-heaven-weaving-new-soul-into-the-loom-of-fate-2nd-ed?p=1434454#post1434454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thematically, it's out of their power. Crafting things into and out of fate is the purview of sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disagree to an extent.<br /> <br /> The &quot;natural state&quot; of stuff in Creation is inside of Fate, so they don't need to actively attach it, you just need to craft it well enough that loom says &quot;oh, hey, that thing belongs in Fate.&quot;<br /> <br /> (Look at it this way. If WST didn't exist and I asked you &quot;can Solar charms create otherwise-ordinary humans that live in Creation and are outside of of Fate&quot;, surely you'd say obviously no, right? If anything WST humans walking around being outside fate and untouched by Creation's system is a bigger flavor violation than having them work themselves into fate, and obviously a bigger problem for Sidereals both mechanically and thematically. If anything, the 1e system - where they just automatically became part of Fate if they spent enough time in Creation, no special stuff required - makes more sense; it should be difficult for Solars to keep an otherwise normal human who lives in Creation <i>outside</i> Fate, probably requiring non-Solar-specific stuff like artifacts or sorcery. Being in Fate is the default and shouldn't generally require a lot of work to obtain provided it's something that logically fits into Creation and spends a lot of time there.)<br /> <br /> But beyond that there's a deeper underlying issue that WST's purpose is to expand Creation. I don't think a splat's charms should generally require assistance from another splat to serve their main purpose. This doesn't necessarily mean that it should be easy or trivial to expand creation with WST, of course, and having support from other Exalted who are experts on what you're trying to create or the systems it's going to be connected to might help, but setting a hard requirement of &quot;Creation can't really get bigger without Sidereal support&quot; is bad.<br /> <br /> Interacting with fate <i>as a central theme</i> should be limited to Sidereals and other fate-themed Exalted, but every type of Exalted can interact with fate in the logical, expected ways creational stuff does as necessary to support their themes, which includes creating stuff and having it be inside it, in the same way that eg. Sidereals aren't the shapeshifting Exalted but still have the ability to turn into a raven as a cool prophet thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 02-20-2021, 11:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-20T02:54:32-08:00","id":1436170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1434428-wyld-shaping-technique-heaven-weaving-new-soul-into-the-loom-of-fate-2nd-ed?p=1434649#post1434649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a <i>somewhat</i> related note:<br /> <br /> The Arczeckhi had the quaint belief that only physical force and spiritual might were real, and only acknowledged someone as a person after they murdered someone else.<br /> <br /> I always felt that their culture could have begun with wyld-shaped people who had been told about the stitch but <i>maybe</i> got a few details wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> interesting twist - I like","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}